# FUTURE_DS_02 - Customer Retention & Churn Analysis

## Project Overview

This project analyzes customer churn and retention patterns for a subscription-based business. The objective was to identify churn drivers, understand customer behavior, and provide recommendations to improve customer retention.

## Tools Used

* Google Sheets
* Pivot Tables
* Charts & Visualizations

## KPIs Analyzed

* Total Customers
* Churn Customers
* Retained Customers
* Churn Rate

## Analysis Performed

* Churn by Contract Type
* Churn by Payment Method
* Average Monthly Charges by Churn Status

## Key Insights

1. Month-to-month contract customers showed the highest churn.
2. Customers using electronic check payment methods churned more frequently.
3. Customers with higher monthly charges were more likely to leave.
4. Long-term contracts improved customer retention.

## Recommendations

1. Offer discounts for yearly subscription plans.
2. Improve customer support for high-risk customers.
3. Introduce loyalty rewards and retention offers.
4. Reduce pricing pressure through bundled plans.

## Outcome

This project enhanced my skills in customer retention analysis, KPI reporting, dashboard creation, and business insight generation using Google Sheets.
